"Library\"},{\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/\",\"title\":\"Bhagavad-gītā As It Is\"},{\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/9/\",\"title\":\"Chapter Nine: The Most Confidential Knowledge\"}],\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/9/12/\",\"bb\":2350,\"has_advanced_view\":false,\"pager\":{\"previous\":{\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/9/11/\",\"title\":\"TEXT 11\",\"has_advanced_view\":false,\"translations\":[\"en\",\"cs\",\"es\",\"bg\",\"pt-br\",\"ru\",\"sk\",\"hr\",\"pl\",\"da\",\"de\",\"et\",\"fr\",\"hu\",\"ko\",\"lt\",\"nl\",\"sl\",\"uk\",\"ja\"]},\"next\":{\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/9/13/\",\"title\":\"TEXT 13\",\"has_advanced_view\":false,\"translations\":[\"en\",\"cs\",\"es\",\"bg\",\"pt-br\",\"ru\",\"sk\",\"hr\",\"pl\",\"da\",\"de\",\"et\",\"fr\",\"hu\",\"ko\",\"lt\",\"nl\",\"sl\",\"uk\",\"ja\"]}},\"child_items\":[{\"section\":\"devanagari\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.devanagari\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"content.DevanagariRecord\",\"title\":\"devanagari\",\"id\":2652,\"bb\":568219,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/9/12/devanagari/\",\"body_final\":\"मोघाशा मोघकर्माणो मोघज्ञाना विचेतस: ।
राक्षसीमासुरीं चैव प्रकृतिं मोहिनीं श्रिता: ॥ १२ ॥\"}]},{\"section\":\"verse_text\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.verse-text\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"verse_text\",\"id\":2653,\"bb\":2351,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/9/12/b2351/\",\"body_value\":\"moghāśā mogha-karmāṇo
mogha-jñānā vicetasaḥ
rākṣasīm āsurīṁ caiva
prakṛtiṁ mohinīṁ śritāḥ\"}]},{\"section\":\"synonyms\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.synonyms\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"books.Synonyms\",\"title\":\"synonyms\",\"id\":2654,\"bb\":2352,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/9/12/b2352/\",\"shadow_value\":\"mogha-āśāḥ – baffled in their hopes; mogha-karmāṇaḥ – baffled in fruitive activities; mogha-jñānāḥ – baffled in knowledge; vicetasaḥ – bewildered; rākṣasīm – demonic; āsurīm – atheistic; ca – and; eva – certainly; prakṛtim – nature; mohinīm – bewildering; śritāḥ – taking shelter of.\",\"word_for_word_value\":[{\"word\":\"mogha-āśāḥ\",\"translation\":\"baffled in their hopes\"},{\"word\":\"mogha-karmāṇaḥ\",\"translation\":\"baffled in fruitive activities\"},{\"word\":\"mogha-jñānāḥ\",\"translation\":\"baffled in knowledge\"},{\"word\":\"vicetasaḥ\",\"translation\":\"bewildered\"},{\"word\":\"rākṣasīm\",\"translation\":\"demonic\"},{\"word\":\"āsurīm\",\"translation\":\"atheistic\"},{\"word\":\"ca\",\"translation\":\"and\"},{\"word\":\"eva\",\"translation\":\"certainly\"},{\"word\":\"prakṛtim\",\"translation\":\"nature\"},{\"word\":\"mohinīm\",\"translation\":\"bewildering\"},{\"word\":\"śritāḥ\",\"translation\":\"taking shelter of\"}]}]},{\"section\":\"translation\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.translation\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"translation\",\"id\":2655,\"bb\":2353,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/9/12/b2353/\",\"body_value\":\"Those who are thus bewildered are attracted by demonic and atheistic views. In that deluded condition, their hopes for liberation, their fruitive activities, and their culture of knowledge are all defeated.\"}]},{\"section\":\"purport\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.purport\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"paragraph\",\"id\":2656,\"bb\":2354,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/9/12/b2354/\",\"body_value\":\"$25\"},{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"paragraph\",\"id\":2657,\"bb\":2355,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/9/12/b2355/\",\"body_value\":\"It is a great offense, therefore, to consider Kṛṣṇa, the Supreme Personality of Godhead, to be an ordinary man. Those who do so are certainly deluded because they cannot understand the eternal form of Kṛṣṇa. The Bṛhad-viṣṇu-smṛti clearly states:\"},{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"verse_text\",\"id\":2658,\"bb\":2356,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/9/12/b2356/\",\"body_value\":\"yo vetti bhautikaṁ dehaṁ
kṛṣṇasya paramātmanaḥ
sa sarvasmād bahiṣ-kāryaḥ
śrauta-smārta-vidhānataḥ
mukhaṁ tasyāvalokyāpi
sa-celaṁ snānam ācaret\"},{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"paragraph\",\"id\":2659,\"bb\":2357,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/9/12/b2357/\",\"body_value\":\"“One who considers the body of Kṛṣṇa to be material should be driven out from all rituals and activities of the śruti and the smṛti. And if one by chance sees his face, one should at once take bath in the Ganges to rid himself of infection.” People jeer at Kṛṣṇa because they are envious of the Supreme Personality of Godhead. Their destiny is certainly to take birth after birth in the species of atheistic and demoniac life. Perpetually, their real knowledge will remain under delusion, and gradually they will regress to the darkest region of creation.\"}]}],\"short_title\":\"Bg. 9.12\",\"medium_title\":\"Bhagavad-gītā As It Is 9.12\"},\"locale\":\"en\",\"activeView\":\"$6:props:activeView\"}]}],\"$L26\",\"$L27\",\"$L28\"]}]\n"])self.__next_f.push([1,"2a:I[83068,[\"/_next/static/chunks/130enlymdm.jk.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0b6f_zxj9ay~6.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/143cg6c13uly6.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/07vk.k35-e~ti.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0j6k6n9cniknh.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0.zxv9arc6a56.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/00-zmo-3n1bt8.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0p4z5tusn0jt6.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/01mcazkjru_is.js\"],\"default\"]\n30:I[78455,[\"/_next/static/chunks/130enlymdm.jk.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0b6f_zxj9ay~6.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/143cg6c13uly6.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/07vk.k35-e~ti.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0j6k6n9cniknh.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0.zxv9arc6a56.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/00-zmo-3n1bt8.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0p4z5tusn0jt6.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/01mcazkjru_is.js\"],\"default\"]\n26:[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"px-4 py-4 w-full max-w-screen-xl mx-auto md:px-8 mb-3\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"nav\",null,{\"aria-label\":\"Breadcrumb\",\"className\":\"breadcrumb mb-8 text-base\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"ol\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"li\",\